                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Honestly I don't have much good to say about Edna & Harvey Breakout, and thats why I cant recommend playing it, even for most staunch fans of p&c adventure genre\r\n\r\nOne small positive this game has is protagonist, Edna. I actually liked Edna as a protagonist more then Lily in Harveys New Eyes, and not just because Edna actually talks. Edna has this sort of weird kid vibe, that doesnt feel like a caricature nor feels too undercooked. I KNEW a girl like Edna in Uni, so I think Breakout succeeded in writing Edna's character. I loved Edna's dialogue, her reactions to the world, and her voice actress was also great, also I love how the game doesn't depict her as being too crazy, or too sane, so as you play the game you keep wondering IF she deserves mental help, or is actively gaslight by people like Dr. Marcel.\r\n\r\nSecond small positive are jokes. They don't hit as hard as best Harvey's New Eyes jokes, but there is probably more variety of jokes here, plus they don't overuse one joke type too many times.Yeah, and thats about it for positives. Everything else is meh, story is meh, music is alright but gets overused a lot and doesnt stand out too much. but the gameplay...\r\n\r\n The Gameplay was just outright frustrating, bordering on moon logic at times, but most frustration came from how the game can waste your time with some item puzzles. Breakout also has traditional mini game puzzles but those sucked too unlike Harveys New Eyes mini games.\r\n\r\nSo unless you're a mega Daedalic fan, and got this game through a Daedalic bundle, I would recommend skipping this game, or at least play Harvey's New Eyes first, since that game felt like a more complete package.",
